BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cutter's Way (1981)
DTSTART:20251002T023000Z
DTEND:20251002T043500Z
DTSTAMP:20251002T023000Z
UID:qtwPkKjkGg
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 109 mins (1h49m)\n\nL.A. Noir: Shadows in Paradise P
 resented by Greg Olson Productions This great film of the 1980s features a
  lazily charming Jeff Bridges as a blue-eyed beach boy who seduces older w
 omen for money and dabbles in selling yachts. He flows along\, easy going\
 , but his crippled\, boozy war vet friend (John Heard) burns red-hot with 
 anger over his own shortcomings and “the sins of the world.” Heard is 
 an “Ahab” looking for a "Moby-Dick” to pursue\, and his target becom
 es an oil tycoon (Stephen Elliott) who Bridges thinks he may have seen dis
 pose of a dead teenage girl in a nocturnal mist. Heard disregards Bridges
 ’ uncertainty and devises a scheme to expose Elliott as “the killer.
 ” But Bridges can’t commit to acting out his friend’s “fantasy.”
  Heard’s long-suffering wife (Lisa Eichorn) sways between the husband sh
 e loves and Bridges\, who’s touched by her melancholy allure. Bridges' a
 cting artistry is quietly stunning as\, alone with Eichorn\, he acknowledg
 es his attraction to her with fond looks and few words. Bridges is the guy
  “who always walks away.” But when a Zen moment of existential choice 
 arises\, young blue eyes can handle it. Presented on 35mm. Individual Tic
 kets: $15Passes: Prorated\, with discounts for SIFF\, SAM\, Swedish Club\,
  UW Cinema Studies\, NWFF\, SFI\, TheFilmSchool\, Festa Italiana\, Allianc
 e Francaise de Seattle\, Scarecrow Video\, & KING FM members\n\nhttps://ww
 w.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/la-noir-shadows-in-paradise/cutters-way\n\nE
 stimated start: 2:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
